  route: term/legacy-jsa-custody-availability
  title: Legacy JSA availability during custody
  type: Concept
  description: In captured DMG 24185–24186, custody or temporary release prevents the availability
    condition and the person is not entitled to legacy JSA(Cont) or JSA(IB). This is an
    entitlement-condition mechanism, not a universal payment-only suspension. DMG 24187 has a
    limited availability treatment for specified custody for a maximum of 96 hours before release,
    so long as the person is not a prisoner. The old suggestions about IS/partner claims and Memo
    07/20 are historical source context, not current application advice.
  status: draft
  authority: model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed-specialist-review-required
